          "id": "57fc3d36-069b-3dfd-91cd-61fdb3ad744f",
          "content": {
            "id": "57fc3d36-069b-3dfd-91cd-61fdb3ad744f",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Big 3 automakers scaling back EV plans for 2026",
            "description": "<p>The Big 3 automakers Ford (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/F\">F</a>), General Motors (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GM\">GM</a>), and Stellantis (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/STLA\">STLA</a>) are all paring back their plans for EVs in 2026. Earlier this week, Ford announced<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/ford-takes-195b-charge-in-hybrid-pivot-cancels-f-150-lightning-ev-launches-new-battery-storage-business-210713166.html\"> major pivots toward hybrid vehicles</a> for 2026 while cutting its F-150 Lightning electric pickup line.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance senior autos reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/pras-subramanian/\">Pras Subramanian</a> outlines the performance of each automaker's EV segments.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
